          <h1>Engineers</h1>
          <p>An engineer is anyone in the field answering workflows on WhatsApp. They don't need an app, a login, or a laptop &mdash; just a phone with WhatsApp.</p>

          <h2>Adding</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>Click <strong>+ Add engineer</strong> on the dashboard.</li>
            <li>Enter their name and mobile number (defaults to UK +44; use the picker for other countries).</li>
            <li>Click <strong>Add</strong>. They receive a WhatsApp intro message.</li>
          </ol>

          <h2>What the engineer sees</h2>
          <p>A normal WhatsApp chat. When you send a workflow, they get something like:</p>
          <div class="callout" style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', monospace;">
            <strong>Quickler</strong><br>
            Hi Tom &mdash; Acme Gas has asked you to run the <em>Annual Safety Check</em> at 14 Station Road. Ready to start? Reply YES when you're on site.
          </div>
          <p>Questions arrive one at a time. The engineer replies with text, numbers, photos, or voice notes. When finished, the report is generated and emailed to you.</p>

          <h2>Removing</h2>
          <p>Click the <strong>&#x2715;</strong> next to their name. Active runs finish but no new ones can be sent. Historical data is kept so reports remain complete.</p>

          <h2>Seats</h2>
          <p>Each plan caps active engineers. The dashboard shows seats remaining. To add more, upgrade your plan.</p>
          <hr style="margin-top:40px;border:none;border-top:1px solid rgba(15,23,42,0.08);">
          <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:#64748b;">
            Still stuck? Email <a href="mailto:hello@quickler.co">hello@quickler.co</a> &mdash; we reply within one business day.
          </p>
